I can't remember when I started this one. It was not too long after
coming sooo close with the previous oddly-named-for-a-woman Hank the
Valk. Standard combat wombat at first. I got a Djinni wish (in
minetown, I think) which I used for SDSM. I usually think in terms of
GDSM + "oR, but this time, I thought I would try to get the [CoMR (I
ended up using a wish in the Castle) 

One issue that came up with abjuring early MR for me was stumbling
into each and every poly trap the RNG saw fit to throw my way (and
probably some it did not). Fortunately, I had found, early on, a ring of
poly control. I became a "new woman" several times.

I Polymorphed Phil the Cat into Phil the Winged Gargoyle in the
big room level. Imagine my embarrassment when he proceeded to eat the
shopkeepers in all of the stores I came across, and the priest in the
minetown temple (I was miffed at that last one). I hated to see all
that gold (and, in one case, all those cool potions) go to waste, so I
collected them.

I had bought about 6 points of protection from the minetown priest
(before I acidentally let Phil eat him), which I managed to lose via a
helm of opposite alignment. Around that time, I also lost Phil to a
level teleport, and he became peaceful. I felt like I was doomed
(DOOOMED!!!) That was right before I got my SDSM, at which point my
morale perked up.

With all the shopkeepers gold and the Ludios loot, I had about $90k,
which I put to good use with the priest in the Valley of the
Dead. Between that and the earlier completion of my armor via the
Castle WoW, the rest was autopilot. I was at AC -41, ~450 HP (crept up
to 490 by quaffing all healing potions upon finding them),
twoweaponing +6 Mojo and a +7 silver sabre.

I did have some fun using one of my wishes for 3 cursed genocide
scrolls and having a major party with about 20-30 nurses. I added
something like 150 HP with that.

For this first time only, I will indulge myself and give the painful
details:

